window.docContents[216].resolve({"/Gamma-Function/5___2-Definitions-and-conventions/#LMLF-___-Mathematical-Functions-with-Lean--Gamma-Function--5___2-Definitions-and-conventions":{"contents":"Qualitative view.The complex and real Mathlib Gamma functions agree on real inputs. At nonpositive integers, the\ntotalized Lean function has value zero; this records an implementation convention at classical poles,\nnot a finite classical Gamma value.Quantitative view.These are exact convention and identification theorems, so a quantitative remainder analogue is not\napplicable.#check LMLF.Definitions.gamma_ofReal\n#check LMLF.Definitions.gamma_neg_nat_eq_zero\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · Mathematical Functions with Lean\u0009Gamma Function","header":"5.2. 5.2 Definitions and conventions","id":"/Gamma-Function/5___2-Definitions-and-conventions/#LMLF-___-Mathematical-Functions-with-Lean--Gamma-Function--5___2-Definitions-and-conventions"}});